(400412, 33610, 10218, '<td valign="top">The purple stuff... that would be fire.  Very wide range of temperatures in that fire up there, and the colors they created were just amazing.<br/> <br/>Edit-<br/>Also, I wasn''t really that close the fire.  I was maybe a 1/4 mile away at closest, and upwind of a relatively small fire.  There are a few trees you can pick out for some size comparison.  One of the easier ones is next to that hot spot just right of the pole at the very bottom.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-27 00:22:06.</i></td>', 'The purple stuff... that would be fire.  Very wide range of temperatures in that fire up there, and the colors they created were just amazing. Edit-Also, I wasn''t really that close the fire.  I was maybe a 1/4 mile away at closest, and upwind of a relatively small fire.  There are a few trees you can pick out for some size comparison.  One of the easier ones is next to that hot spot just right of the pole at the very bottom.', '2003-08-27 01:16:25.000000', '2003-08-27 01:22:06.000000', 0),
(400413, 34046, 1, '<td valign="top">Wowsa.  Beautiful image.  My only complaint is that it seems distorted.. though that''s mostly the effect the sand meeting the water has on my eyes.</td>', 'Wowsa.  Beautiful image.  My only complaint is that it seems distorted.. though that''s mostly the effect the sand meeting the water has on my eyes.', '2003-08-27 01:16:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(400414, 34041, 7711, '<td valign="top">Phillippe!<br/> <br/>I was just looking at the challenge finishes since I didn''t vote. I''m shocked to see you received NO comments on this, yet you must be wondering why this score. I like this shot for the following reasons:<br/> <br/>the colours remind of the parched colours of summer, and the lines and dots of green bushes break up the monotone.<br/> <br/>The problems I see with it are: <br/> <br/>there isn''t a significant point of interest and not enough in the shapes and lines we do see to keep attention. Its just sort of a background without a subject.<br/> <br/>Overall, I think its a great effort for your first entry, congratulations on your socre, and I hope to see more from you soon! :) Don''t be discouraged at the lack of comments, either! If all else fails, ask for some in the forums. Many people are happy to oblige.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-27 12:14:30.</i></td>', 'Phillippe! I was just looking at the challenge finishes since I didn''t vote. I''m shocked to see you received NO comments on this, yet you must be wondering why this score. I like this shot for the following reasons: the colours remind of the parched colours of summer, and the lines and dots of green bushes break up the monotone. The problems I see with it are:  there isn''t a significant point of interest and not enough in the shapes and lines we do see to keep attention. Its just sort of a background without a subject. Overall, I think its a great effort for your first entry, congratulations on your socre, and I hope to see more from you soon! :) Don''t be discouraged at the lack of comments, either! If all else fails, ask for some in the forums. Many people are happy to oblige.', '2003-08-27 01:16:59.000000', '2003-08-27 13:14:30.000000', 0),
(400416, 34179, 9893, '<td valign="top">underrated! this screams summer =)</td>', 'underrated! this screams summer =)', '2003-08-27 01:17:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(400417, 33584, 9027, '<td valign="top">congrats!</td>', 'congrats!', '2003-08-27 01:18:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(400418, 34263, 9893, '<td valign="top">I loved this one... I''m sad to see it didn''t do better!</td>', 'I loved this one... I''m sad to see it didn''t do better!', '2003-08-27 01:19:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(400420, 34301, 7291, '<td valign="top">HEY!!! You copied my Post Card submition!  LOL!  Check out my profile if you haven''t seen it.  Well, yours scored better than mine.  Great shot!</td>', 'HEY!!! You copied my Post Card submition!  LOL!  Check out my profile if you haven''t seen it.  Well, yours scored better than mine.  Great shot!', '2003-08-27 01:19:59.000000', NULL, 0),
