(401733, 34102, 4380, '<td valign="top">im so surprised with the ranking, it should be on the top ten pix. and i totally disagreed that this is out of focus..i really love the way you captured this bugs..still congrats and  be proud of your submission...i really dont know about the 1 and 3 ratings.</td>', 'im so surprised with the ranking, it should be on the top ten pix. and i totally disagreed that this is out of focus..i really love the way you captured this bugs..still congrats and  be proud of your submission...i really dont know about the 1 and 3 ratings.', '2003-08-27 16:29:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(401774, 33970, 806, '<td valign="top">I saw this photo due to Mavrik''s post in the forums. I did not vote this challenge as I was on vacation.<br/> <br/>This is an excellent shot. The colors and quality are vibrant. The dof works well to show proper depth, and the position of the boy to the man tells many stories, and creates a leading line from the boy to the man.<br/> <br/>A shot you should be proud of!</td>', 'I saw this photo due to Mavrik''s post in the forums. I did not vote this challenge as I was on vacation. This is an excellent shot. The colors and quality are vibrant. The dof works well to show proper depth, and the position of the boy to the man tells many stories, and creates a leading line from the boy to the man. A shot you should be proud of!', '2003-08-27 17:09:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(401790, 34041, 11263, '<td valign="top">Thanks a lot for the post-challenge comments and to frisca for PMing me about them.<br/> <br/>To be honest it was a bit disappointing to get no feedback whatsover at the end of the challenge and you''re definatly a nice bunch to have taken the time to do it.<br/> <br/>It was not possible to put some sky in there, there are hills and a gulf in the background, the sky is too far.<br/> <br/>Image sharpness : I forgot to sharpen the image before submitting it and my camera tends to produce soft images indeed.<br/> <br/>I think I could have gotten a bit more depth of field with a smaller aperture but the fact that everything seems to be on the same plane is probably due to the zoom factor I used (this is a really cropped part of the original picture)<br/> <br/>Cheers</td>', 'Thanks a lot for the post-challenge comments and to frisca for PMing me about them. To be honest it was a bit disappointing to get no feedback whatsover at the end of the challenge and you''re definatly a nice bunch to have taken the time to do it. It was not possible to put some sky in there, there are hills and a gulf in the background, the sky is too far. Image sharpness : I forgot to sharpen the image before submitting it and my camera tends to produce soft images indeed. I think I could have gotten a bit more depth of field with a smaller aperture but the fact that everything seems to be on the same plane is probably due to the zoom factor I used (this is a really cropped part of the original picture) Cheers', '2003-08-27 17:37:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(401813, 33397, 10676, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who voted for my picture, 20th out of 262 Im well pleased. Thanks again</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who voted for my picture, 20th out of 262 Im well pleased. Thanks again', '2003-08-27 17:50:45.000000', NULL, 0),
