(404979, 34104, 11312, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. <br/>I agree, with them. Apart from the photo being taken in the summer, it doesent really suggest it at all. I was just so excited at joining DPC that I wanted to "jump in" straight away, and this was the only shot that fitted the posting criteria. I hope to be submitting more suitable efforts in the future.<br/>Tao</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I agree, with them. Apart from the photo being taken in the summer, it doesent really suggest it at all. I was just so excited at joining DPC that I wanted to "jump in" straight away, and this was the only shot that fitted the posting criteria. I hope to be submitting more suitable efforts in the future.Tao', '2003-08-30 23:59:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(405245, 34259, 772, '<td valign="top">Hi Tina...<br/> <br/>I scored this photo a 6, which means it''s slightly above an avarage photo, but not much.  The scene you chose here is nice, but there is nothing of particularly strong interest to look at.  It is a simple outdoor landscape scene with no strong focal point for the viewer.  I don''t know how this particular scene could be improved much, especially under the rules of this particular challenge.  A scene like this one often takes a bit of ''time of day'' research to determine when the best LIGHT is for the shot :)  Photography is all about looking for the light.  The light will determine whether a scene like this one is strong or just mediocre :)</td>', 'Hi Tina... I scored this photo a 6, which means it''s slightly above an avarage photo, but not much.  The scene you chose here is nice, but there is nothing of particularly strong interest to look at.  It is a simple outdoor landscape scene with no strong focal point for the viewer.  I don''t know how this particular scene could be improved much, especially under the rules of this particular challenge.  A scene like this one often takes a bit of ''time of day'' research to determine when the best LIGHT is for the shot :)  Photography is all about looking for the light.  The light will determine whether a scene like this one is strong or just mediocre :)', '2003-08-31 16:41:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(406179, 34301, 5475, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by K-Rob:</b></div><hr/><i>HEY!!! You copied my Post Card submition!  LOL!  Check out my profile if you haven''t seen it.  Well, yours scored better than mine.  Great shot!</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi K-Rob,<br/>No, I did not know you had a Garden of the Gods shot at the time!  But since I got a 4th, i think I''ll look through your portfolio for some more shots to ''copy''.  This one worked out well, so I''ll trust your judgement and follow your lead again!  LOL<br/>JD</td>', 'Originally posted by K-Rob:HEY!!! You copied my Post Card submition!  LOL!  Check out my profile if you haven''t seen it.  Well, yours scored better than mine.  Great shot!  Hi K-Rob,No, I did not know you had a Garden of the Gods shot at the time!  But since I got a 4th, i think I''ll look through your portfolio for some more shots to ''copy''.  This one worked out well, so I''ll trust your judgement and follow your lead again!  LOLJD', '2003-09-01 12:29:05.000000', NULL, 0),
